## Reproducibility

The project uses:

```python
RANDOM_STATE = 42
```

The same random state is shared by:

- Train/test splitting
- Cross-validation
- Model initialization
- Hyperparameter search

For a clean validation run:

```text
Kernel → Restart Kernel and Run All Cells
```

---

## Current Limitations

- CSV files only
- Tabular supervised learning only
- No time-series handling yet
- No grouped-data split strategy
- No automatic leakage detection yet
- No model-drift monitoring yet
- No web interface yet
- Large one-hot encoded datasets may consume significant memory
- Hyperparameter tuning may be slow on limited hardware

